/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Most organisations are not failing. They continue investing in technology, transformation, governance, talent and growth. Many remain profitable, continue expanding and appear successful by conventional measures. Yet beneath that success, a quieter pattern is emerging.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Leaders increasingly describe organisations that are becoming harder to move. Decisions require more coordination, initiatives demand greater alignment, dependencies multiply and transformation efforts overlap. The organisation remains active, yet progress often feels slower than expected.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
